<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sodom and Gomorrah</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sodom and Gomorrah are two cities of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebrew-bible">Hebrew Bible</a>, described in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/book-of-genesis">Book of Genesis</a> as destroyed by God with fire and brimstone for the wickedness of their inhabitants. Their location, traditionally placed near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dead-sea">Dead Sea</a>, is unknown. In the 1970s claims that the tablets of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ebla">Ebla</a> mentioned them were widely publicised, but most scholars later rejected these readings.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sodom-and-gomorrah.jpg" alt="Sodom and Gomorrah" width="320" height="204" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: John Martin · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:John_Martin_-_Sodom_and_Gomorrah.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
